query:
OCAPI shop API call from a customer's middleware is 401ing. they've been on this integration for years and it just started failing -- here's the exact request and the OCAPI fault envelope:

curl -X GET 'https://zzrf-001.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com/s/RefArch/dw/shop/v23_2/customers/abc12345' \
  -H 'x-dw-client-id: aaaaaaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd-eeeeeeeeeeee' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer some-old-token-string'

response: HTTP 401
body:
{
  "fault": {
    "type": "AuthenticationFailedException",
    "message": "The access token is invalid."
  }
}

what does the OCAPI shop customers spec actually require for auth here? trying to figure out if the token shape changed or if their client config drifted
